From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 06:40:01 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] domicile: a tooltip is drawn inside the window it is over


A desktop on a tty lost its GPU process about two minutes in, on a page in a
browser window:

    FATAL:ui/ozone/platform/drm/gpu/gbm_surface_factory.cc:355
      DCHECK failed: thread_checker_.CalledOnValidThread().
    #7 ui::GbmSurfaceFactory::CreateCanvasForWidget()
    #8 viz::OutputSurfaceProviderImpl::CreateSoftwareOutputDeviceForPlatform()

Nothing had disabled GPU compositing. One compositor asked for software:
`TooltipAura::CreateTooltipWidget` sets `force_software_compositing`, and
`DesktopWindowTreeHostPlatform::Init` forces it for any `TYPE_TOOLTIP`.
ozone/drm cannot composite in software, so the root frame sink aborts.

0051 keeps menus and tooltips out of top-level windows, but asks only for
`params.parent`, and a tooltip names none -- `TooltipAura` sets
`params.context`. So a tooltip still got a `DesktopNativeWidgetAura`, its own
compositor and the abort. `NativeWidgetAura` takes a parent or a context
(`DCHECK(params.parent || params.context)`), and with a context
`ParentWindowWithContext` lands a tooltip in the root window, as on ash.

`scripts/test-a-popup-is-drawn-inside-its-window.sh` reads the series for it.

Co-Authored-By: Connor Prussin <connor@prussin.net>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01KHQC9zsRk48yEYB7qPSwwY
---
 .../browser/ui/views/chrome_views_delegate_linux.cc  | 12 +++++++++---
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/chrome/browser/ui/views/chrome_views_delegate_linux.cc b/chrome/browser/ui/views/chrome_views_delegate_linux.cc
index c7a7a46..ead9a9f 100644
--- a/chrome/browser/ui/views/chrome_views_delegate_linux.cc
+++ b/chrome/browser/ui/views/chrome_views_delegate_linux.cc
@@ -90,9 +90,15 @@ NativeWidgetType GetNativeWidgetTypeForInitParams(
   // so that it can leave its parent's bounds, but on a platform that presents
   // only the window filling a display that window is never drawn: on ozone/drm
   // it binds to no CRTC. Draw it in its parent instead, as ash does.
-  if (params.parent && !ui::OzonePlatform::GetInstance()
-                            ->GetPlatformRuntimeProperties()
-                            .presents_every_window) {
+  //
+  // A tooltip names no parent, only a context (TooltipAura), and asks for
+  // software compositing, which ozone/drm cannot do: as a top-level window its
+  // compositor aborts the GPU process in
+  // GbmSurfaceFactory::CreateCanvasForWidget. NativeWidgetAura takes either.
+  if ((params.parent || params.context) &&
+      !ui::OzonePlatform::GetInstance()
+           ->GetPlatformRuntimeProperties()
+           .presents_every_window) {
     return NativeWidgetType::kNativeWidgetAura;
   }
 
